<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What may leave this device, and by which route. Applies from API 31, which
    is this app's minimum, so this file is the whole of the answer.

    The two operations are deliberately answered differently, because they are
    different things wearing the same name:

      - **Cloud backup** copies the app's data to Google's servers, keyed to the
        reader's account, and restores it after an uninstall. Everything is
        excluded. The privacy policy says that what the app remembers is stored
        only on this device and that uninstalling deletes it, and until this
        file said so too, that was not true: Android's default is to back up
        everything, so a reader's saved words — with the sentences they came
        from — their bookmarks, their reading positions and every search they
        had made were going to a server the app never mentions.

      - **Device transfer** moves the data straight to a new phone during a
        migration the reader is standing in front of. Nothing is excluded and no
        section is written for it, which leaves Android's default of carrying
        everything: a vocabulary built up over months should survive changing
        phones, and it never touches anybody's server on the way.

    The cache is not listed because Android never backs it up, which is also why
    a downloaded update cannot end up in either.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
</data-extraction-rules>
